{"v":2,"s":"p","w":5,"steps":[{"t":"read","h":"Free fall","b":"<p><b>Free fall</b> (slobodan pad) is motion under gravity alone, starting from rest. Every body falls with the same acceleration g ≈ 9.81 m/s² (often rounded to 10).</p><div class=\"fx\">v = g·t   h = g·t²/2   v = √(2gh)</div><div class=\"callout\">In 1971 an astronaut dropped a hammer and a feather on the Moon — no air, so they landed together.</div><figure class=\"fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 320 170\" text-anchor=\"middle\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A falling ball photographed once every second (g ≈ 10 m/s²): the gaps grow because the speed keeps growing — h = gt²/2.\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"ink\"/></marker><marker id=\"ahc\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"a\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"160\" class=\"km\" /><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"14\" r=\"8\" class=\"a\"/><line x1=\"76\" y1=\"14\" x2=\"84\" y2=\"14\" class=\"k\" /><text x=\"70\" y=\"18\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\">0 m</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\">t = 0 s</text><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"23\" r=\"8\" class=\"a\"/><line x1=\"76\" y1=\"23\" x2=\"84\" y2=\"23\" class=\"k\" /><text x=\"70\" y=\"27\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\">5 m</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"27\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\">t = 1 s</text><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"50\" r=\"8\" class=\"a\"/><line x1=\"76\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"84\" y2=\"50\" class=\"k\" /><text x=\"70\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\">20 m</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\">t = 2 s</text><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"95\" r=\"8\" class=\"a\"/><line x1=\"76\" y1=\"95\" x2=\"84\" y2=\"95\" class=\"k\" /><text x=\"70\" y=\"99\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\">45 m</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"99\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\">t = 3 s</text><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"158\" r=\"8\" class=\"a\"/><line x1=\"76\" y1=\"158\" x2=\"84\" y2=\"158\" class=\"k\" /><text x=\"70\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\">80 m</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\">t = 4 s</text></svg><figcaption>A falling ball photographed once every second (g ≈ 10 m/s²): the gaps grow because the speed keeps growing — h = gt²/2.</figcaption></figure>"},{"t":"read","h":"Throwing upward","b":"<p>A body thrown up with v₀ slows by g every second:</p><div class=\"fx\">v = v₀ − g·t</div><p>At the top v = 0, so t<sub>up</sub> = v₀/g and h<sub>max</sub> = v₀²/(2g). The way down takes the same time, and it lands with the same speed.</p>"},{"t":"ex","q":"A ball is thrown up at 20 m/s (g = 10 m/s²). When is it at the top, how high, and when does it land?","s":["t_up = 20/10 = 2 s.","h_max = 400/20 = 20 m.","Down takes another 2 s → lands after 4 s."],"a":"2 s, 20 m, 4 s"},{"t":"num","q":"Distance fallen in 5 s (g = 10)?","a":125,"u":"m","e":"10 · 25/2."},{"t":"num","q":"Speed after falling 20 m (g = 10)?","a":20,"u":"m/s","e":"√(2·10·20) = √400."},{"t":"num","q":"Max height when thrown up at 30 m/s (g = 10)?","a":45,"u":"m","e":"900/20."},{"t":"tf","q":"In a vacuum, a heavier body falls faster.","a":false,"e":"All bodies fall with the same g."},{"t":"num","q":"Time to the top when thrown up at 15 m/s (g = 10)?","a":1.5,"u":"s","e":"15/10.","tol":0.01}]}